{"content":[{"c":["KENIZZITES"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["A people related to Kenaz, grandson of Esau (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.11,15","r":"Gen.36.11,15","rawR":"Gen.36.11,15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.11,15","value":"Gen.36.11,15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 36:11, 15"},"). The Kenizzites were of Edomite stock and resided to the southeast of Judah in the vicinity of the Kenites. They are thought to belong to the pre-Israelite population of Canaan (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.15.19","r":"Gen.15.19","rawR":"Gen.15.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.15.19","value":"Gen.15.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 15:19"},"). Their territory was to be given to the Israelites along with that of the Kenites, the Amorites, and the Canaanites (vv ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.15.19-21","r":"Gen.15.19-21","rawR":"Gen.15.19-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.15.19-21","value":"Gen.15.19-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"19-21"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In Numbers and Joshua, Caleb, the faithful spy, is reckoned to belong to the Kenizzites (",{"href":"?bref=Num.32.12","r":"Num.32.12","rawR":"Num.32.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.32.12","value":"Num.32.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 32:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.14.6,14","r":"Josh.14.6,14","rawR":"Josh.14.6,14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.14.6,14","value":"Josh.14.6,14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 14:6, 14"},"). According to ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.15","r":"1Chr.4.15","rawR":"1Chr.4.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.15","value":"1Chr.4.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 4:15"},", Caleb’s genealogy is traced back to Judah (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.1","r":"1Chr.4.1","rawR":"1Chr.4.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.1","value":"1Chr.4.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:1"},"). The relationship of Caleb to the Kenizzites is far from clear. Caleb established his patrimony at Kiriath-sepher (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.1.11-13","r":"Judg.1.11-13","rawR":"Judg.1.11-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.1.11-13","value":"Judg.1.11-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 1:11-13"},"), which is in Judah but which is also situated close to the territory of the Kenizzites. Critical opinion views the Kenizzites as non-Israelites who occupied Hebron, Debir, and the southernmost hill country of the Negev and became politically incorporated into Judah."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Kenizzites","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 36:11, 15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.36.11,15","rawQueryValue":"Gen.36.11,15","sourceRefExact":"Gen.36.11,15"},{"anchorText":"Gn 15:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.15.19","rawQueryValue":"Gen.15.19","sourceRefExact":"Gen.15.19"},{"anchorText":"19-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.15.19-21","rawQueryValue":"Gen.15.19-21","sourceRefExact":"Gen.15.19-21"},{"anchorText":"Nm 32:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.32.12","rawQueryValue":"Num.32.12","sourceRefExact":"Num.32.12"},{"anchorText":"Jos 14:6, 14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.14.6,14","rawQueryValue":"Josh.14.6,14","sourceRefExact":"Josh.14.6,14"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 4:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.4.15","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.4.15","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.4.15"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 4:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.4.1","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.4.1","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.4.1"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 1:11-13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.1.11-13","rawQueryValue":"Judg.1.11-13","sourceRefExact":"Judg.1.11-13"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"578e2f0be31a23de04a5b5bb7ec4ffc8c10b2f35d58d3cb65038c6fa3a537520","sourceItemName":"Kenizzites","sourceItemOrder":44,"sourceMember":"Articles/K.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Kenizzites","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Kenizzites","title":"Kenizzites","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}